# Structured Logging And Observability

- Prefer structured logs over ad hoc string logging.
- Include request ID, tenant ID, route or operation name, severity, and actor context when available.
- Never log secrets, tokens, raw credentials, or unnecessary personal data.
- Reuse request-context helpers and existing monitoring packages instead of inventing parallel logging patterns.
- Errors, security warnings, and background-job failures must be traceable across app, job, and database boundaries.
